description:
Design a dual-edge-triggered signal detection circuit using a flip-flop. The module captures the input signal and produces two outputs: `posedgesig_f`, which indicates a rising edge of the input signal (`sig`), and `negedgesig_f`, which indicates a falling edge. The circuit uses a clock signal (`clk`) for synchronization and a reset signal (`reset`) to initialize the stored value. When `reset` is low, the stored signal is cleared to zero; otherwise, it updates on the rising edge of the clock. The outputs are generated by detecting transitions between the current and previous states of the input signal.
module top_module(clk, reset, sig, posedgesig_f, negedgesig_f
    );

code:
module top_module(clk, reset, sig, posedgesig_f, negedgesig_f
    );input clk, sig, reset;
	 output posedgesig_f, negedgesig_f;

	 reg sig_d;


	 always @ (posedge clk or negedge reset) 

	 if (!reset) begin
		sig_d = 0;
	 end else begin
		sig_d = sig;
	 end 

	 assign posedgesig_f = sig & !sig_d;
	 assign negedgesig_f = !sig & sig_d;

endmodule

