description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input into its equivalent 4-bit Gray code output. The conversion is achieved in two stages: Stage 1 computes intermediate values based on the input, using bitwise XOR operations between adjacent bits, while Stage 2 further processes these intermediate results to produce the final Gray code output. The module ensures that only one bit changes at a time when transitioning between consecutive values in Gray code, which is a key characteristic of this coding scheme.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] data_in,
    output reg [3:0] gray_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] data_in,
    output reg [3:0] gray_out
);reg [3:0] stage1_out;
reg [3:0] stage2_out;

// Stage 1
always @(*) begin
    stage1_out[0] = data_in[0];
    stage1_out[1] = data_in[1] ^ data_in[0];
    stage1_out[2] = data_in[2] ^ data_in[1];
    stage1_out[3] = data_in[3] ^ data_in[2];
end

// Stage 2
